  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Dry weather through next Thursday.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\n1035mb surface high pressure located off of the Delmarva remains\nsouth of the area through the day. This will bring sw flow to \nthe region with local case studies showing this to result in \ndrier dewpoints than fcst by guidance and have subsequently dropped\ndwpt temps into the 20s, based on extremely dry soundings and\npersistence. This likely to result in relative humidities today\ndropping down toward 20%. Given the dry airmass temps should\neasily be able to climb thru the 50s with lower 60s common acrs\nthe area for highs today. \n\nCold front moves through on Monday with a small chance for an \nisolated shower acrs the north before front washes out over \ncentral areas. Have continued idea of 20-30 pops with little in \nthe way of measurable rainfall expected.\n\nHigh pressure builds in quickly following fropa with H8 temps\ndropping toward -9C on Tuesday. Highs on Tuesday will barely\nmake it into the 40s over the north with Wednesday just a few\ndegrees warmer as CWA affected by weak H5 troffing through the\nmiddle of the week.\n\nS/wv ridging likely to bring temps back above normal for\nThursday with a fast-moving s/wv flattening the ridge through\nthe end of the week. There may be off and on rain chances after\nThursday but no significant threat for any real measurable \nrainfall through the end of the month.",
